<h3 style="font-size: 25px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 10px;"><b>Part A: AML, CFT and Legal Framework</b></h3>
<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 1: Introduction to AML, CFT and Proliferation Financing (Weightage: 6%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This foundational unit introduces the dark economy. Candidates will learn how illicit funds are integrated into the legitimate financial system. It covers the three stages of money laundering: Placement, Layering, and Integration. Furthermore, it introduces the global efforts led by the Financial Action Task Force (FATF) to combat the financing of terrorism and the financing of weapons of mass destruction (Proliferation Financing).


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 2: Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002 (PMLA) (Weightage: 8%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
A highly critical chapter carrying significant weight. Candidates must master the definitions and core provisions of the PMLA, 2002. This includes understanding the definitions of proceeds of crime, the powers of the Directorate of Enforcement (ED) regarding attachment and confiscation of property, the establishment of Appellate Tribunals, and the establishment of Special Courts to try PMLA offences.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 3: The Prevention of Money-laundering (Maintenance of Records) Rules, 2005 (Weightage: 8%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Intermediaries are bound by strict record-keeping rules. This module requires mastery of the PMLA Rules, 2005. You must understand the specific obligations of reporting entities, the exact procedures for maintaining records of transactions, the preservation period of such records (typically 5 years), and the mandate to furnish information to the Director of the Financial Intelligence Unit - India (FIU-IND). Using comprehensive NISM XXIV Study Materials is vital for memorising these specific statutory timelines.</p>


<h3 style="font-size: 25px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;"><b>Part B: AML Guidelines and Compliance in Securities Market</b></h3>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 4: Scheduled Offences (Weightage: 3%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This chapter delves into the specific criminal acts that generate the "proceeds of crime." Candidates must understand the structure of the Schedule to the PMLA, which includes offences under the Indian Penal Code (IPC), the Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, the Prevention of Corruption Act, and various other cross-border legislations.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 5: AML, CFT and PF Guidelines (Weightage: 5%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This section bridges the gap between the law and practical guidelines. It covers the overarching principles of creating an effective AML/CFT compliance programme within a financial institution. It touches upon the appointment of a Principal Officer and a Designated Director, and the necessity of independent audits to test the efficacy of the AML framework.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 6: SEBI Guidelines for AML Standards, CFT and PF (Weightage: 7%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
As an employee in the securities market, SEBI's master circulars are your primary operational directive. This chapter evaluates your understanding of SEBI’s specific mandates for registered intermediaries. It covers the formulation of written AML procedures, the Risk-Based Approach (RBA) to client categorization (Low, Medium, High Risk), and the handling of alerts generated by internal surveillance systems. Practising with an NISM AML and CFT Provisions in Securities Markets Certification Model Test will heavily test your knowledge of these specific SEBI directives.</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 7: KYC Norms in Securities Market (Weightage: 8%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Client onboarding is the first line of defence. This highly operational chapter requires mastery of the Know Your Customer (KYC) norms. You must understand the role of KYC Registration Agencies (KRAs), the Central KYC Records Registry (CKYCR), and the process of identifying the Ultimate Beneficial Owner (UBO) for non-individual clients (like corporate entities, trusts, and partnerships). It also covers Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) protocols for Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs) and Non-Profit Organisations (NPOs).</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 8: Discussion on PMLA Related Cases (Weightage: 5%)</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
The final chapter grounds the legal theory in reality. It explores past case studies, regulatory orders, and real-world examples of money laundering within the securities market. Candidates must analyse how intermediaries failed in their compliance duties and the resulting punitive actions taken by regulators. Testing yourself with an NISM AML and CFT Provisions in Securities Markets Certification Demo Test ensures you understand the practical application of these legal precedents.
</p>


